{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1514","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1514","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1514\",\"parent_revision\":\"37c5591f3b5b4688cf5481cad5c10c6f97c0e388\",\"root_revision\":\"39a89adb5fb5d0c743c75c1245bd6a29dbaa8d5a9cf2aa7a4b5ee27312e182ac\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nLocalYamlTaskProvider.create_plan detects duplicate plan conditions by parsing exception message strings (e.g., checking if \\\"already exists\\\" appears in str(exc)). String message parsing is fragile \u2014 message text changes silently break the detection logic and produce incorrect behavior without any test failure. The code review identified this as a brittleness introduced during P912.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nPARTIALLY CORRECTED \u2014 the original Fact-Check contained an inaccurate claim. Updated analysis below.\\n\\nVERIFIED \u2014 `local_yaml.py:261\u2013273` catches `ValueError` from `query.create_plan` and checks `\\\"already exists\\\" in str(exc)` to distinguish error types.\\n\\nCORRECTED \u2014 the original claim that `query.py:133\u2013141` raises `ValueError` with `\\\"Plan P{plan_number} already exists\\\"` is WRONG. `query.create_plan` uses UUID4-derived plan IDs (`P` + first 8 hex chars) and prevents filesystem collision via a 3-attempt loop, raising `OSError` on UUID exhaustion \u2014 not `ValueError` with any \\\"already exists\\\" message.\\n\\nThe only place a `ValueError` with \\\"already exists\\\" in its message could appear is `_utils.py:39`:\\n```python\\nraise TaskValidationError(0, f\\\"Task ID {task.id!r} already exists in plan {plan_id!r}\\\")\\n```\\nBut `TaskValidationError` is NOT a `ValueError` \u2014 it is a `SamError`. It is also raised by `validate_appended_task`, not by `query.create_plan`.\\n\\nActual code path:\\n- `query.create_plan` raises `ValueError` only for task model validation failures (Pydantic): `f\\\"Task at index {i} failed validation: {exc}\\\"`\\n- `local_yaml.py:267`'s `\\\"already exists\\\" in msg` check matches a message that `query.create_plan` can NEVER emit \u2014 it is dead code\\n- `PlanExistsError` is therefore never reachable through the `local_yaml.py` ValueError handler for the duplicate-plan scenario\\n\\nEvidence:\\n- `local_yaml.py:261\u2013273` \u2014 the fragile string-matching catch\\n- `query.py:86\u2013116` \u2014 UUID-based plan ID generation; raises `OSError` for UUID collision; raises `ValueError` only for Pydantic task validation errors\\n- `_utils.py:38\u201339` \u2014 `TaskValidationError` (not `ValueError`) for duplicate task IDs\\n- `exceptions.py:37\u201347` \u2014 `PlanExistsError` defined but never raised by the `local_yaml.py` ValueError handler in practice\\n\\nThe defect is therefore two-fold:\\n1. `local_yaml.py:267`'s `\\\"already exists\\\"` check is dead code \u2014 it cannot be triggered because `query.create_plan` never raises `ValueError` with that substring\\n2. The `TaskBackend` Protocol documents `PlanExistsError` for `create_plan`, but the `LocalYamlTaskProvider` implementation can never surface it through this path\\n\\nThe `sam_create` MCP tool (which calls `backend.create_plan`) thus silently fails to raise `PlanExistsError` for any scenario.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nType: defect (fragile error detection via string parsing instead of typed exceptions)\\n\\nRoot-Cause Analysis:\\n1. `query.create_plan` raises bare `ValueError` for both duplicate-plan and invalid-task errors\\n2. `ValueError` is the only signal available to the caller \u2014 no typed exception hierarchy in the query layer\\n3. `local_yaml.py` distinguishes the two cases by string matching, coupling to message text\\n4. `PlanExistsError` exists in `exceptions.py` but is not raised by the query layer directly\\n5. No test asserts the exact `ValueError` message format, so a message change would be silent\\n</div>\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/local_yaml.py:255\u2013267` \u2014 fragile string-matching catch\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/query.py:133\u2013141` \u2014 raises bare `ValueError` for duplicate plan\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/exceptions.py:37\u201347` \u2014 `PlanExistsError` already defined, needs to be raised at source\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nIf `query.py` error message text changes (routine refactor, internationalisation, or wording improvement), duplicate-plan detection silently breaks. The second `create_plan` call for a duplicate plan raises `TaskValidationError` instead of `PlanExistsError`. Callers that catch `PlanExistsError` to handle the duplicate case will not catch it. Severity: medium (silent misbehavior on duplicate plan creation, affects `sam_create` MCP tool).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nNone \u2014 fix is self-contained within `query.py` and `local_yaml.py`. Can land independently of #1513.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] `query.create_plan` raises a typed exception (not bare `ValueError`) for the duplicate-plan case \u2014 either `PlanExistsError` directly, or a new `PlanCollisionError` that `local_yaml.py` can catch by type\\n- [ ] `local_yaml.py:create_plan` no longer uses `\\\"already exists\\\" in str(exc)` \u2014 it catches a typed exception by class\\n- [ ] The fix uses Python's typed exception hierarchy (`except PlanExistsError` or equivalent), NOT `cast()`, `Any`, or message parsing\\n- [ ] `query.py` may raise `ValueError` for task-validation failures (acceptable \u2014 those are already re-raised as `TaskValidationError` from a regex match); the duplicate-plan path must be a typed exception\\n- [ ] A test covers: calling `create_plan` twice with the same issue number raises `PlanExistsError` (not `TaskValidationError`, not `ValueError`)\\n- [ ] `uv run prek run --files local_yaml.py query.py` passes with zero lint/type errors after the change\\n</div>\\n\\n## Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nEstimate: S\\nReasoning: Change `query.create_plan` to raise `PlanExistsError` directly (one line), update `local_yaml.py` to catch `PlanExistsError` by type (replaces 3-line string check), add one test. Low risk \u2014 typed exception is strictly more correct than string matching.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Reproducibility\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n```python\\n# Rename \\\"already exists\\\" to \\\"already present\\\" in query.py line 138, then:\\nbackend = LocalYamlTaskProvider(plan_dir)\\nbackend.create_plan(slug=\\\"test\\\", goal=\\\"g\\\", tasks=[...], issue=42)\\nbackend.create_plan(slug=\\\"test\\\", goal=\\\"g\\\", tasks=[...], issue=42)  # duplicate\\n# \u2192 raises TaskValidationError(0, \\\"Plan P42 already present: ...\\\") instead of PlanExistsError\\n# \u2192 caller sees wrong exception type, wrong behavior silently\\n```\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **localyamltaskprovider.create_plan parses exception messages as strings \u2014 fragile error detection** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: QG T1 code review of P912 \u2014 follow-up plan P1430\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-05\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n\\n---\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-24)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- The `TaskBackend` Protocol contract (`create_plan` raises `PlanExistsError` for duplicate plans) is not implemented by `LocalYamlTaskProvider` \u2014 callers relying on that contract get silent data duplication instead\\n- `sam_plan(action='create')` MCP callers that pass the same `issue` or `slug` twice receive two distinct plan files with no error \u2014 duplicate plans accumulate in the plan directory silently\\n- `PlanExistsError` is caught by `server.py` handlers; since it is never raised, those handlers are also dead code\\n- The string `\\\"already exists\\\" in str(exc)` couples the detection logic to a message format that does not exist in the actual raise site \u2014 any future refactor that accidentally introduces a matching ValueError would trigger false-positive `PlanExistsError` raises\\n- Severity: medium \u2014 silent plan duplication on repeated `sam_create` calls for the same issue; affects the `dh:planning` skill and anything that calls `sam_plan create`\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nWhen the fix is complete, the observable target state is:\\n\\n- Calling `LocalYamlTaskProvider.create_plan()` twice with the same `issue` number raises `PlanExistsError` on the second call \u2014 no second YAML file is written.\\n- `LocalYamlTaskProvider.create_plan()` no longer contains a `\\\"already exists\\\" in str(exc)` string check \u2014 the detection is purely type-based.\\n- `query.create_plan()` raises a typed exception (not bare `ValueError`) when a plan collision is detected \u2014 the caller does not need to inspect the exception message.\\n- The `memory.py` and `local_yaml.py` backends behave consistently: both raise `PlanExistsError` for duplicate plan creation; the `TaskBackend` Protocol contract is satisfied by all concrete implementations.\\n- `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/ -x -q` and `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/ -x -q` pass with a new test that asserts `PlanExistsError` is raised (not `TaskValidationError`, `ValueError`, or silent success) on a duplicate `create_plan` call.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] `LocalYamlTaskProvider.create_plan` raises `PlanExistsError` when a plan file for the same `issue` number already exists in `plan_dir` (scan by `issue` field in existing YAML files, or by slug collision)\\n- [ ] The detection uses file-system inspection or a typed exception path \u2014 NOT `\\\"already exists\\\" in str(exc)`\\n- [ ] `local_yaml.py:267`'s dead-code `\\\"already exists\\\" in msg` branch is removed\\n- [ ] `query.create_plan` or `create_plan_file` raises a typed exception (e.g. `PlanExistsError` directly, or a new internal `PlanCollisionError`) when a same-issue plan already exists, so the caller does not need string parsing\\n- [ ] `memory.py` backend's `create_plan` is reviewed to confirm its `PlanExistsError` path is reachable (as a reference implementation)\\n- [ ] A test covers: calling `create_plan` twice with the same `issue` number raises `PlanExistsError` from `LocalYamlTaskProvider` (not `TaskValidationError`, not `ValueError`, not silent success)\\n- [ ] `uv run prek run --files plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/local_yaml.py plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/query.py` passes with zero lint/type errors\\n- [ ] `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/ -x -q` passes\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\nNone \u2014 fix is self-contained within `query.py` and `local_yaml.py`. Can land independently of #1513.\\n\\nBlocks: None identified.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nEstimate: S\\nReasoning: The fix requires (1) adding duplicate-plan detection in `query.create_plan` or `LocalYamlTaskProvider.create_plan` by scanning existing YAML files for matching issue number, (2) raising `PlanExistsError` directly, (3) removing the dead-code string-check branch, (4) adding one test. All changes are in two files. Low risk \u2014 typed exception is strictly more correct than dead string-matching code.\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/local_yaml.py:261\u2013273` \u2014 dead-code `\\\"already exists\\\" in str(exc)` branch in `create_plan`; the `PlanExistsError` raise is unreachable\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/query.py:46\u2013116` \u2014 `create_plan` uses UUID4 IDs; no duplicate-plan detection; raises `ValueError` only for Pydantic task validation failures\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/exceptions.py:37\u201347` \u2014 `PlanExistsError` defined correctly; needs to be raised at source\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/_utils.py:38\u201339` \u2014 `TaskValidationError` for duplicate task IDs (note: NOT `ValueError`, so cannot be matched by the ValueError catch)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/memory.py:227\u2013233` \u2014 reference implementation; confirm `PlanExistsError` path is reachable\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\nThe string-matching branch at `local_yaml.py \u2014 LocalYamlTaskProvider.create_plan()` (lines 265\u2013273) is the sole code path affected. Every caller that reaches this branch expects `PlanExistsError` to be raised for duplicate plans; because the branch is dead code, those callers never observe the error.\\n\\n**Direct callers that catch `PlanExistsError`:**\\n- `sam_schema/server.py \u2014 _sam_plan_create()` calls `backend.create_plan()`; FastMCP converts `SamError` subclasses into `ToolError`. Since `PlanExistsError` is never raised by `LocalYamlTaskProvider`, the MCP tool silently succeeds and returns a new plan ID instead of signalling a duplicate.\\n\\n**Indirect callers (anything that calls `sam_plan create`):**\\n- The `dh:planning` skill \u2014 creates plans via `sam_plan(action='create', issue=N)`. A second call with the same issue number currently creates a second, distinct YAML file rather than raising an error.\\n- Any agent or test that calls `backend.create_plan()` and expects `PlanExistsError` on a repeat call gets silent success instead.\\n\\n**Reference implementations unaffected:**\\n- `memory.py \u2014 InMemoryTaskProvider.create_plan()` raises `PlanExistsError` correctly (line 235\u2013236) \u2014 this is the reference implementation.\\n- `beads.py \u2014 BeadsTaskProvider.create_plan()` raises `PlanExistsError` correctly (lines 559\u2013561).\\n\\n**Protocol contract gap:**\\n- `task_backend.py \u2014 TaskBackend.create_plan()` documents `PlanExistsError` in its docstring. The `LocalYamlTaskProvider` implementation violates this contract silently \u2014 no runtime error, no type error.\\n\\n**Scope of the fix:**\\n- `query.py \u2014 create_plan()`: add duplicate-plan detection (scan by `issue` field or slug match in existing YAML files) and raise `PlanExistsError` directly, OR add a new internal typed exception for the collision case.\\n- `local_yaml.py \u2014 LocalYamlTaskProvider.create_plan()`: remove the dead `\\\"already exists\\\" in str(exc)` branch; catch the typed exception by class.\\n- `exceptions.py \u2014 PlanExistsError`: no changes needed; already correctly defined.\\n- Tests: `tests/test_task_backend_conformance.py` and/or `tests_sam/` \u2014 add a test asserting that a duplicate `create_plan` call raises `PlanExistsError`.\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n```python\\n# Demonstrate that \\\"already exists\\\" check is dead code:\\n# Call create_plan twice with identical issue number\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nfrom sam_schema.core.backends.local_yaml import LocalYamlTaskProvider\\nfrom sam_schema.core.exceptions import PlanExistsError\\nfrom sam_schema.core.models import Task\\n\\nprovider = LocalYamlTaskProvider(plan_dir=Path(\\\"/tmp/test_plans\\\"))\\ntask = Task.model_validate({\\\"id\\\": \\\"T1\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"test\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"not-started\\\"})\\n\\nprovider.create_plan(slug=\\\"test\\\", goal=\\\"g\\\", tasks=[task], issue=42)\\n# Second call: because UUID4 is used, this creates a DIFFERENT file \u2014 no collision, no error\\n# PlanExistsError is never raised regardless of issue number reuse\\nprovider.create_plan(slug=\\\"test\\\", goal=\\\"g\\\", tasks=[task], issue=42)\\n# \u2192 Two distinct plan files are created; neither raises PlanExistsError\\n```\\n\\nThe string-matching dead code can also be demonstrated by verifying no ValueError with \\\"already exists\\\" is ever raised by query.create_plan:\\n```bash\\nuv run python -c \\\"\\nimport ast, inspect\\nfrom sam_schema.core import query\\nsrc = inspect.getsource(query.create_plan)\\nprint('already exists in source:', 'already exists' in src)\\n\\\"  # \u2192 False\\n```\\n\",\"digest\":\"20a38e1699d4f43bb5ce691f747ca1aa45207b32819f50f4f92a4a40d30e7fdd\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg40VQ\"}"}